in American history,

00:37:30.690 --> 00:37:33.240
these are the outcomes that
have led from those events.

00:37:33.240 --> 00:37:34.500
What you guys are saying is

00:37:34.500 --> 00:37:36.240
we're then adding prescriptive statements,

00:37:36.240 --> 00:37:38.310
which is, that's why you
should never really try

00:37:38.310 --> 00:37:40.260
because you'll never
make it in this country.

00:37:40.260 --> 00:37:41.370
- That's not what I'm saying.

00:37:41.370 --> 00:37:44.220
What I am saying is that if you negatively

00:37:44.220 --> 00:37:49.220
press a child with these thoughts,
that will be the outcome.

00:37:49.410 --> 00:37:51.990
Because that's how human beings work.

00:37:51.990 --> 00:37:54.569
This is a psychological fact.

00:37:54.569 --> 00:37:55.560
(object thwacks softly)

00:37:55.560 --> 00:37:57.501
- [Ragini] The quality of education

00:37:57.501 --> 00:37:59.501
is the government's job.

00:38:07.530 --> 00:38:08.940
- I believe it is the government's job.

00:38:08.940 --> 00:38:11.250
Look, our funding comes
through government.

00:38:11.250 --> 00:38:13.110
I mean, our schools are
government entities.

00:38:13.110 --> 00:38:14.040
So it is-
- Policies.

00:38:14.040 --> 00:38:16.020
- Policies are government,
everything's gov.

00:38:16.020 --> 00:38:17.700
I mean, if you're in public education,

00:38:17.700 --> 00:38:18.533
you're in government.

00:38:18.533 --> 00:38:19.620
That's, we're bureaucrats.

00:38:19.620 --> 00:38:20.790
That's literally what our job.

00:38:20.790 --> 00:38:22.740
So it is government's job.

00:38:22.740 --> 00:38:25.397
So yeah, I believe it is the job

00:38:25.397 --> 00:38:28.860
of the government because
schools are government.

00:38:28.860 --> 00:38:29.880
That's literally what they are.

00:38:29.880 --> 00:38:31.530
They're government institutions.

00:38:31.530 --> 00:38:32.880
- Yes, I completely agree.

00:38:32.880 --> 00:38:36.300
Government provides a
certain quality to education.

00:38:36.300 --> 00:38:38.460
Obviously, they haven't
provided those funds,

00:38:38.460 --> 00:38:39.930
they haven't provided those policies

00:38:39.930 --> 00:38:41.970
that are pro-teacher
or anything like that.

00:38:41.970 --> 00:38:46.970
So it really shows in our
education, in kids, in all around,

00:38:47.160 --> 00:38:51.330
we're just not at the quality
that other countries are at.

00:38:51.330 --> 00:38:53.034
- Yeah.
(object thwacks softly)

00:38:53.034 --> 00:38:57.060
(footfalls thud loudly)

00:38:57.060 --> 00:38:59.610
- I was going back and forth
because what a government is,

00:38:59.610 --> 00:39:00.990
you know, oftentimes is characterized

00:39:00.990 --> 00:39:04.320
as like this entity of like
a group of people up there

00:39:04.320 --> 00:39:05.550
deciding what goes on,

00:39:05.550 --> 00:39:08.160
where, no, like government is
just collective organization.

00:39:08.160 --> 00:39:10.380
Does a government have a role
in education, absolutely.

00:39:10.380 --> 00:39:12.750
I think that parents have
to play a role as well

00:39:12.750 --> 00:39:14.250
and you know, not only being involved

00:39:14.250 --> 00:39:16.290
with what their kid is learning in school,

00:39:16.290 --> 00:39:20.610
but also, you know, reinforcing
strong educational skills.

00:39:20.610 --> 00:39:22.590
And that doesn't happen unless
there is parent involvement.

00:39:22.590 --> 00:39:25.230
I know the kids that are
being worked on at home

00:39:25.230 --> 00:39:26.550
versus the kids that aren't.

00:39:26.550 --> 00:39:28.080
And it plays out in test scores.

00:39:28.080 --> 00:39:30.030
It plays out in their engagement in class.

00:39:30.030 --> 00:39:31.560
And it plays out in their behavior.

00:39:31.560 --> 00:39:32.393
- You have to remember

00:39:32.393 --> 00:39:33.870
that we're a representative government,

00:39:33.870 --> 00:39:35.430
that it's based on the people, right.

00:39:35.430 --> 00:39:37.140
And so these public school systems

00:39:37.140 --> 00:39:39.060
are waiting for the
parents to come in and say,

00:39:39.060 --> 00:39:41.220
this curriculum is not
what I wanna teach my kids.

00:39:41.220 --> 00:39:43.500
We, the taxpayers, control the curriculum.

00:39:43.500 --> 00:39:45.900
But the problem is we haven't
been engaging in that system

00:39:45.900 --> 00:39:47.490
because we've been so distracted

00:39:47.490 --> 00:39:50.760
and pulled away from the
education from our kids.

00:39:50.760 --> 00:39:53.040
- No, I would agree,
communities need to absolutely

00:39:53.040 --> 00:39:54.690
be more involved in their school boards

00:39:54.690 --> 00:39:55.860
and what's going on in education.

00:39:55.860 --> 00:39:57.120
And unfortunately, we don't have that.

00:39:57.120 --> 00:40:00.330
And oftentimes, a lot of
politicians, albeit Republicans,

00:40:00.330 --> 00:40:02.520
that are trying to cut
a lot of social programs

00:40:02.520 --> 00:40:03.930
and a lot of social investment,

00:40:03.930 --> 00:40:05.130
as well as corporate democrats

00:40:05.130 --> 00:40:07.110
who want to cut a lot
of social investment,

00:40:07.110 --> 00:40:09.480
both of those, you know,
we see areas of corruption

00:40:09.480 --> 00:40:10.830
within our education system.

00:40:10.830 --> 00:40:12.030
- Well, and let's be clear

00:40:12.030 --> 00:40:13.740
on what we're talking about government is.

00:40:13.740 --> 00:40:17.190
So when we talk about on a
local level, it is government.

00:40:17.190 --> 00:40:18.600
That's literally what government is.

00:40:18.600 --> 00:40:20.370
When your kid goes into the school,

00:40:20.370 --> 00:40:22.080
they're going into a
government institution.

00:40:22.080 --> 00:40:23.910
So I think when we are talking,

00:40:23.910 --> 00:40:25.530
we're not talking about
parents not being involved.

00:40:25.530 --> 00:40:26.363
I want you involved.

00:40:26.363 --> 00:40:27.720
Heck, please be involved.

00:40:27.720 --> 00:40:29.850
So I think our issue, when we
were talking about government,

00:40:29.850 --> 00:40:31.440
we're not talking about excluding parents.

00:40:31.440 --> 00:40:33.450
We're talking about it is government's job

00:40:33.450 --> 00:40:37.110
to make this entity, which is
public education, function.

00:40:37.110 --> 00:40:37.943
It has to.

00:40:37.943 --> 00:40:40.230
If government's not
involved, you have no money.

00:40:40.230 --> 00:40:42.750
- So you guys teach in government
schools, public schools,

00:40:42.750 --> 00:40:45.570
essentially you're teaching
a diverse student body.

00:40:45.570 --> 00:40:48.150
You have conservatives, you have liberals.

00:40:48.150 --> 00:40:51.210
How can you better represent
us, half of this country?

00:40:51.210 --> 00:40:54.000
It's sadly causing us to
lose faith in you guys.

00:40:54.000 --> 00:40:55.050
We wanna support you guys,

00:40:55.050 --> 00:40:57.210
we wanna send our kids to your
schools and your classrooms.

00:40:57.210 --> 00:40:59.520
- And I think that when we talk
about all these differences,

00:40:59.520 --> 00:41:02.400
you know, how do we sort of represent

00:41:02.400 --> 00:41:03.420
both of these sides, right?

00:41:03.420 --> 00:41:04.560
How do we bring these people together?

00:41:04.560 --> 00:41:06.270
I think it's also really
important to remember

00:41:06.270 --> 00:41:09.390
that, historically, this
curriculum is one sided

00:41:09.390 --> 00:41:12.360
in favor of conservative views,

00:41:12.360 --> 00:41:14.850
in favor of supporting White students,

00:41:14.850 --> 00:41:16.430
not students of color, right.

00:41:16.430 --> 00:41:18.390
And so I think that we
really, as a country,

00:41:18.390 --> 00:41:20.130
need to take a look at
our education system.

00:41:20.130 --> 00:41:21.450
I think we can all agree that

00:41:21.450 --> 00:41:23.610
there needs to be a lot of
change in the system, right.

00:41:23.610 --> 00:41:25.140
And look at how we can build a system

00:41:25.140 --> 00:41:28.290
that represents, reflects, validates

00:41:28.290 --> 00:41:31.147
the experiences and
identities of everybody.

00:41:31.147 --> 00:41:32.179
- Wonderful.
- Beautiful.

00:41:32.179 --> 00:41:33.175
(all clapping loudly)

00:41:33.175 --> 00:41:34.376
That was good, girl.

00:41:34.376 --> 00:41:37.543
(mellow serene music)

